Mechanisms
- crates/bbt-proto/src/messaging.rs: MessageKind::class derives conversation/event from the signed kind. No sender-selectable class field; Presence is event and the existing Task stays conversation.
- Six new kind/body pairs carry exactly the pinned fields: SlotClaimed, SlotReleased, CutClaimed, Landed, GateResult, TaskTransition. LandingTier, GateStage and GateVerdict are typed. Machine event bodies expose no model text.
- WakeMode declares wake/inbox/digest. Receipt.wake is optional; absent legacy rows emit no new fields. New states encode flat wake=now/none or wake=deferred plus until. The decoder refuses unknown/partial states. Until is the RFC 3339 string carried on the wire; deadline production and interpretation remain in the host's later policy/digest cut.
- crates/bbt-mux/src/messaging/wire.rs: SendRequestExt::validate refuses every new kind with event_input_unavailable before host admission; typed bodies cannot masquerade under an old kind. Existing conversation validation remains.
- crates/bbt-mux/src/messaging/ledger.rs: existing receipt construction adds wake: None.
- crates/bboxy450-term/src/messaging.rs: exhaustive labels cover the six new kinds.

Compatibility
- All 37925 prior golden bytes are an exact prefix of the updated file, SHA-256 d73fe83c99b80dcb914e5f4182d56bc7b4ef899bd048e62d9157c085859436ce.
- 17 cases appended: six event bodies; remaining gate verdicts; legacy text, presence and task bodies; legacy absent wake; now, none and deferred wake states.
- No envelope field or signing format changed. The signed kind still determines its class. No producer, policy store, digest scheduler, native delivery behaviour, GUI or catalogue change.

